<title>USA: Navistar says UAW votes on contract extensio.</title>
<headline>Navistar says UAW votes on contract extensio.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Navistar International Transportation Corp said on Sunday 63.0 percent of United Auto Workers (UAW) members voted on ratification of a proposed master contract extension.</p>
<p>The company said in a press statement, however, that a deal had yet to be finalised.</p>
<p>The company also said UAW ratified issues pertaining to the Next Generation Truck.</p>
<p>The UAW did not ratify a measure to cut costs at the Indianapolis foundry, the company said.</p>
<p>Navistar and the UAW reached a tentative agreement on Wednesday to extend the master contract, which covers about 8,000 employees.</p>
</text>
